- Story & Context: In the mythic aftermath of the Galleria raids, legend holds that the final movement was performed by an automated loop left running across twelve arcade circuit boards and an unattended, mechanically vibrating concert harp while the building was sealed with plywood. Local skate kids broke back in weeks later to find the mall’s great four-story dome tinted blood-red by the setting sun, the entire concrete structure vibrating with an unearthly, symphonic surf tremolo that sounded like an orchestra drowning in open water. Scribbled with grease-pencil on the glass of a melted Galaga screen was the band's departing epitaph: "leave the high score burning in the sea."
